  "issue_id": "rock_issue:SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6919",
  "diagnosis_status": "maintainer_confirmed",
  "diagnosis_summary": "Public Rock 19.2 source used a shared mutable Dictionary cache in the singleton AzureBlobStorageClient and performed an unsynchronized ContainsKey/Add sequence. A Rock maintainer added a concurrent regression test, confirmed that it reproduced the reported race, replaced the cache with ConcurrentDictionary.GetOrAdd, and closed the issue. The issue is labeled Fixed in v19.4; verify exact package inclusion because a release-line label is not an exact build attestation.",
  "workaround_summaries": [
    "Use a Rock build proven to contain commit d66a4f492306b10c7bd71aa13d54273918c941a3. Until upgraded, an application-pool recycle may restore service after the reported failure, but it does not remove the concurrency defect and is not a durable fix."
  ],
